        "date": "2026-11-20T20:34:37Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): judge the first traverse of the rotary, multi-axis and cross-drill kinds\n\nAfter a tool change the post sends Z, then X/Y at that height, then the\nrotary words. The #2901 law skipped the rotary, multi-axis and\ncross-drill kinds, so their first traverse posted unjudged.\n\n- sim::verify::first_traverse_low_swept: a rotary kind reads its work\n  and the steel that turns with it swept through a full turn about the\n  fitted axis, the fixed steel as it stands, and the start at its\n  machine height over the axis line.\n- The multi-axis kinds and the cross drill on a mill answer to the\n  #2901 tip law in the part frame.\n- The op stamp of those kinds takes one more word, so a cache judged\n  without the law reads Stale once.\n\nDecision: docs/decisions/2965-first-traverse-rotary.md.\n\nFixes #2965\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
