  {
    "sha": "05c9e56f271478eb03e5d9ee873822aa2bdedad3",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDA1YzllNTZmMjcxNDc4ZWIwM2U1ZDllZTg3MzgyMmFhMmJkZWRhZDM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-20T21:49:34Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-20T21:49:34Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app): read the table on a 3+2 plane only where the axial move can go under it\n\nThe 3+2 first-traverse law read the machine table's top face along the\ntool axis. Along a horizontal axis (B 90) the table's far X edge read as\na high \"top\", so a B 90 pocket on tilthead.mch at clearance Z95 was\nrefused \"under the fixture top Z625\", and the multiaxis-indexed catalog\ncase \"under the fixture top at Z500\". A move along a horizontal axis\nkeeps the world Z: those refusals were false.\n\ntable_read now takes the worst start on the table top face and asks if\nthe move along the tool axis to the plane can drop the tool more than\nZ_TOL under the table top. An up-pointing axis counts the table then\nand names the top face's highest reading. A horizontal axis never\ncounts it. An axis that points down toward the table (past 90 deg) gets\na note, because the verdict can only say \"raise\", which is wrong there.\n\nPinned by first_traverse_table::a_horizontal_head_axis_does_not_read_the_far_table_edge,\n::a_near_horizontal_head_axis_still_reads_the_table and\n::a_head_tilt_past_90_names_the_table_unjudged (replaces the B 120 pin,\nwhich read the wrong side of the face for such an axis).\n\nRefs #2987\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
